Allow overriding ckb-vm's MSVC-branch asm compiler via CKB_VM_ASM_CC.

ckb-vm 0.24.14's build.rs assembles src/machine/asm/execute_x64.S as part
of the `asm` / `detect-asm` feature path.  The file is written in GNU AT&T
syntax, which Microsoft's ml64.exe (MASM) cannot parse, so the author
hardcoded `build.compiler("gcc")` for the is_msvc branch under the
assumption that a native Windows MSVC developer has a GNU gcc.exe from
MinGW-w64 available alongside cl.exe.

This assumption breaks for cross-compilation from Linux to
x86_64-pc-windows-msvc: "gcc" resolves to the host's Linux gcc, which
cannot emit MSVC COFF objects and also chokes on cc-rs's MSVC-style
`/imsvc<path>` flags supplied via CFLAGS_x86_64_pc_windows_msvc.

Fix: honour an optional CKB_VM_ASM_CC env var.  When set, build.rs uses
that compiler instead of "gcc"; when unset, the existing native-Windows
behaviour is preserved.  The Guix build sets CKB_VM_ASM_CC to clang-cl,
which handles GNU AT&T .S files natively via LLVM's integrated assembler
and produces valid MSVC-ABI COFF.

diff --git a/build.rs b/build.rs
index 1f7e9e0..9dd181c 100644
--- a/build.rs
+++ b/build.rs
@@ -35,12 +35,17 @@ fn main() {
         if x64_asm {
             build.file("src/machine/asm/execute_x64.S");
             if is_msvc {
-                // For now, only an assembly source code is required for CKB-VM, we won't
-                // need to build any C source file here. Hence we can use this simpler solution
-                // to set the default compiler to GCC. We will need to manually trigger the
-                // command to assemble the assembly code file, should any C source file is also
-                // required here.
-                build.compiler("gcc");
+                // On native Windows an MSVC developer usually has a GNU gcc
+                // installed alongside, so the default is to route the GNU-
+                // syntax .S file through "gcc".  When cross-compiling from
+                // Linux (where "gcc" is the host's Linux cc and can't emit
+                // MSVC COFF), callers can point at clang-cl via this env var
+                // instead — clang-cl handles GNU AT&T assembly natively.
+                if let Ok(cc) = env::var("CKB_VM_ASM_CC") {
+                    build.compiler(cc);
+                } else {
+                    build.compiler("gcc");
+                }
             }
         } else if aarch64_asm {
             build.file("src/machine/asm/execute_aarch64.S");
